+# Incidents brief
+
+Action status as of the 30 September on-call meeting.
+
+## 11 August: ingest stall and full disk
+
+- **Impact:** Data stopped arriving for about 2.5 hours overnight; customers saw stale dashboards. No data was lost.
+- **Root cause:** One malformed batch trapped the ingest pipeline in an endless retry loop; the retry logs filled the database disk, halting writes.
+- **Fix:** Restart setting the bad batch aside, then freeing database space and pruning old logs.
+- **Follow-ups:**
+  - Disk alert at 80% full: Sunil, done.
+  - Stop bad batches jamming the pipeline: Jonas, open (in review).
+  - Paging escalation rules: Elif, done.
+
+## 21 September: expired API certificate
+
+- **Impact:** Public API unreachable for 47 minutes on Monday morning; nearly all customer connections failed.
+- **Root cause:** The API's security certificate expired; its automatic renewal had failed silently since early September, holding an outdated credential.
+- **Fix:** Certificate renewed, API restarted; renewal job repaired, now alerts on failure.
+- **Follow-ups:**
+  - Reminder 14 days before each expiry: Priya, done.
+  - Alert on days left: Priya, open.
+  - Expiry check in the weekly checklist: Tomasz, open.
+  - Responders record their steps during incidents: Mara, done.
